# SQL Server conventions (FsCore)

- Target is SQL Server 2019. There is no `REGEXP`, `RLIKE` or `REGEX_LIKE`. For whole-word matching call `dbo.fn_ContainsWholeWord(@text, @word)`; do not hand-roll `LIKE '%word%'`, which matches substrings.
- Check column names against `INFORMATION_SCHEMA.COLUMNS` or `db/migrations/` before using them.
- Name list columns explicitly. No `SELECT *` in procs.
- Store and compare instants as `datetime2` in UTC. Never use `GETDATE()`; use `SYSUTCDATETIME()`.
- Procs are read-only unless the ticket says otherwise: no `INSERT`, `UPDATE`, `DELETE` in a `usp_Get*` proc.
- Escape `%`, `_` and `[` before any user text goes into a `LIKE` pattern.
- Proc name `dbo.usp_Get<Noun>By<Filter>`. One proc per SOAP operation.
- tSQLt tests live in `db/tests/<ProcName>/`. Create fixtures inside the test (tSQLt rolls back) and prefix any object you create with `tsqlt_`.
